acore has outraised her substantially and joined the DCCC's Red to Blue program, running on healthcare costs in a district Democrats nearly won in past cycles.\n\nMost professional raters place the race between Lean R and Likely R, with a couple calling it a tossup, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-four chance. Public polling is sparse and mostly Democratic-sponsored, showing a near-tied race, so the Republican edge is real but not commanding. Expect a competitive race with Honeycutt favored.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2812, "margin": -3.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2869, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3426, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2761, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3368, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2774, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2992, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2787, "margin": -4.0}]}